{
  "_": [
    "Accessories found in Paillard's own dated dealer price lists.",
    "",
    "Same source and the same discipline as data/lens-items/listings.json:",
    "the dealer price lists scanned by Pacific Rim Camera, read back against",
    "the page one row at a time rather than matched by script. asPrinted is",
    "the document's own wording.",
    "",
    "Where a code appears in more than one list the prices are all kept, so",
    "the entry shows what the thing cost over time. A few went up between",
    "1965 and 1967 and a few did not move at all.",
    "",
    "addCodes gives the accessory Paillard's five-letter code, which the",
    "original site never recorded for any of them.",
    "",
    "",
    "A trap in the two 1970s lists, written down because it would publish a",
    "dealer's cost as a shop price. October 1976 prints its columns as",
    "Dealer Cost then Suggested Retail. January 1978 prints them the other",
    "way round, Suggested Retail then Dealer Net. Everything here is the",
    "retail figure, which is the second number in the 1976 list and the",
    "first in the 1978 one. Both headers were read off the rendered page.",
    "",
    "Re-run scripts/extract-accessory-items.mjs after editing."
  ],
